==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Kroxo]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[Scissoroo]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Bun Bun Symbiote]] spawns as the boss.
**10 [[Kroxo]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
**5 [[Scissoroo]]s spawn, delay 30~36.67 seconds<sup>900f~1,100f</sup>.
**1 [[I.M. Phace]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Another stage full of [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] enemies, just like [[2nd Round: Dawn (Expert)]] and [[4th Round: Dawn (Deadly)]], you will need [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]], except this time you will basically need every single [[Aqua Crystal]] and [[Plasma Crystal]] [[Treasure]] from each [[Into the Future]] chapter. In other words, you need basically all [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] in order for this stage to become managable for the average player. Starts very similarly to [[Galactic Threat (Merciless)|Galactic Threat]], except there is only one Scissoroo, making it much easier to stall. When the base is hit, 10 more Kroxos and 5 more Scissoroos appear with Bun Bun Symbiote and an I.M. Phace. If you've beaten [[Metabolic Syndrome]] before, this will be a cakewalk, if not, then you will need to use the [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] cats in your lineup that you've most likely brought for the other stages. [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] and other [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield]] units are useful for nullifying Bun Bun Symbiote's [[Wave Attack|wave]] RNG dealing massive damage to, or killing an entire stack of units.

